sentences.t:
“Levantados en pie, ya Çid Campeador,
besad las manos, ca los pie[de]s no;
si esto non feches, non avredes mi amor.”

sentences.l:
“Raise-yourself on foot, O Çid Campeador,
kiss the hands, for the feet no;
if this not you-do, not you-will-have my love.”

sentences.t:
Dixo el rey: “esto feré d'alma e de coraçón;
aquí vos perdono e dovos mi amor,
ên todo mio reyno parte desde oy.”

sentences.l:
Said the king: “this I-will-do from-soul and from heart;
here you I-pardon and I-give-you my love,
and-in all my realm part from today.”

sentences.t:
Otro día mañana, claro salie el sol,
el Campeador a los sos lo mando
que adobassen cozina pora quantos que i son;

sentences.l:
Other day morning, bright was-coming-out the sun,
the Campeador to the his it ordered
that they-should-prepare kitchen for as-many-as that there are;
